@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", end="!\n")
+
+Unlike print and log, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop output, apply console markup, or replace emoji codes. Markup-like text and emoji codes are written literally.
+
+``out`` does apply automatic highlighting by default, and accepts a ``style`` argument, which is applied in the same way as print. Pass ``highlight=False`` to disable highlighting for a call, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+
+
